          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+completion"} analytic completion
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+ring"}> localization of a ring
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+commutative+ring"} localization of a commutative ring
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion+of+a+module"} completion of a module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+scheme"} formal scheme
          %h2#references References
          %p A classical account is in section 1 of
          %ul
            %li#Sullivan05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"}> Dennis Sullivan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric topology: localization, periodicity and Galois symmetry
              %p
                by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Ranicki"} Andrew Ranicki
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/books/gtop.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p Brief surveys include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Completion_%28ring_theory%29"} Completion (ring theory)
            %li#Bridges11
              %p
                Brett Bridges,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An introduction to ring completions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uwo.ca/~srankin/courses/4123/2011/brett_presentation.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            of adic completion (“Greenless-May duality”) is in
          %ul
            %li#GreenleesMay92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"}> John Greenlees
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Derived functors of I-adic completion and local homology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/73.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Leovigildo Alonso, Ana Jeremías,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Lipman"} Joseph Lipman
                %em Local Homology and Cohomology on Schemes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9503025"}> arXiv:alg-geom/9503025
                )
            %li#PortaShaulYekutieli10
              %p
                Marco Porta, Liran Shaul,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amnon+Yekutieli"} Amnon Yekutieli
                %em On the Homology of Completion and Torsion
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1010.4386"}> arXiv:1010.4386
                )
          %p
            for more on this see also at
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/fracture+theorem#CompletionAndTorsionOnDerivedCategories"} fracture theorem – Arithmetic fracturing for chain complexes
          %p
            Discussion of interrelation between completion and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+morphisms"} etale morphisms
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Leovigildo Alonso, Ana Jeremias, Marta Perez,
              %em Local structure theorems for smooth maps of formal schemes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0605115"}> arXiv:math/0605115
              )
          %p
            Discussion of formal completion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-modules"} (infinity,1)-modules
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totalization"} totalization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amitsur+complexes"} Amitsur complexes
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Carlsson07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gunnar+Carlsson"}> Gunnar Carlsson
              ,
              %em Derived completions in stable homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0707.2585"}> arXiv:0707.2585
              )
          %p Completion for complex cobordism theory is in
          %ul
            %li#GreenMay97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"}> John Greenlees
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %em Localization and Completion Theorems for MU-Module Spectra
